{% comment %}
  sections/testimonials.liquid
  
  A row of customer reviews that starts against a filled intro panel and runs
  off the right-hand edge of the page.

  ## The surface is `sections/feature-cards.liquid`'s, setting id for setting id

  Colour scheme, background media, the four border widths, the opacity slider,
  the two radii, the margins, the container, the gaps, the animation family —
  every id here is the one that section already carries, and both reach them
  through `snippets/spacing.liquid`, `snippets/background-media.liquid` and
  `snippets/container.liquid` rather than reimplementing them. A merchant who
  has set up a Feature cards section has set up this one.

  The carousel is the same too. `carousel-shell-attrs` and `carousel-shell-tail`
  supply the attributes and the controls from the same sub-snippets
  `carousel-shell.liquid` itself uses, so the arrows, the peek, the pause button
  and the live region are one implementation across all three sections. The
  element is written out here rather than rendered through the shell because
  its slides are theme blocks and `{% content_for %}` output cannot be captured
  — theme-check reports it as an error, because Shopify renders blocks with
  their editor bindings attached and buffering that into a variable is not
  something the platform supports.

  ## Two layouts, and the bleed belongs to one of them

  The same Type select and **Carousel on mobile** pair as
  `sections/feature-cards.liquid`, with the default the other way round: this
  row is drawn as a slider against a fixed panel, so Carousel is what it ships
  as, and Grid wraps the cards into columns beside the panel instead.

  The bleed is resolved per breakpoint rather than once. A carousel that runs
  off the side of the page is an affordance — a half-visible card says there is
  more this way. A *grid* that does it is a row with its last column cut in half
  and no way to reach it. So Grid at a breakpoint drops the bleed at that
  breakpoint, and the arrows and the progress bar stand down with it.

  ## Why the row runs off the edge

  `.testimonials__track` cancels the container's end padding with a negative
  margin, using the same `max()` expression `.container__bleed` reads back — so
  it lands on the true viewport edge at every breakpoint and every container
  width, rather than guessing a gutter.

  Only the end side. Bleeding both would put the first card under the intro
  panel; bleeding neither would end the row on the container line, which reads
  as the last card being cut off by a margin rather than as more cards existing.
  A half-visible card at the screen edge is the affordance — it says "there is
  more this way" without a single arrow being drawn.

  It is a setting rather than a constant because the section is also usable
  inside a narrow column, where a track that escapes its parent is a bug.

  ## The intro panel is a static block, outside the carousel

  `{% content_for 'block', type: '_testimonial-intro' %}`, the same mechanism
  `sections/feature-cards.liquid` uses for its heading cluster. Inside the track
  it would be a slide: it would scroll away on the first arrow press, and Swiper
  would count it when deciding whether the merchant's Loop setting is
  achievable. Outside it, it holds its column and the reviews move past it.

  `--tc-intro-width` is published by the block and read by the grid here, so the
  panel's own width slider drives the section's column template. The block owns
  its box; the section owns where the box sits.

  ## The controls are outside the track, and that is why the id exists

  Rendered under the row rather than inside `<swiper-carousel>`, because the
  track bleeds off the screen and controls inside it would go with it — arrows
  set to Outside would end up beyond the viewport edge.

  `detached: true` on `carousel-shell-tail` keeps the pause button and the live
  region, which are found by ref and announced from inside the element, and
  stands the arrows and the pagination down so they can be drawn below instead.
  They reach the carousel through `data-carousel-for`, which is what `id:` on
  `carousel-shell-attrs` is for. The id is the section's, so two of these on one
  page cannot claim each other's controls.

  ## The cards arrive one at a time

  One `<motion-effect>` around the track with `data-target=".testimonial-card"`
  and a stagger, rather than an effect on each card. A card is a merchant block
  — `{% content_for 'blocks' %}` renders them all in one call and passes no
  index — so there is no `forloop.index0` to turn into a per-card delay.
  Targeting rather than `data-children` is deliberate: once Swiper mounts it
  moves the cards into a wrapper of its own, and a selector still finds them
  where a child list would not.

  ## Nothing clips

  A card's product disc hangs past the bottom of the card on purpose. So the
  track carries `--tc-thumb-overhang` worth of padding underneath it rather than
  `overflow: hidden` anywhere, and Swiper's own wrapper is left visible in
  `base.css`.

  ## Migration note

  This section used to take the theme's public `testimonial` block. It now takes
  `_testimonial-card`, which is a different shape — a product, a verified badge
  and a hover panel that the old block has no settings for. `blocks/testimonial.liquid`
  is untouched and still works wherever else it is used.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings

  assign desktop = s.columns_desktop | default: 3 | plus: 0

  comment
    Mobile columns is a select of two, clamped rather than trusted — a section
    saved at three before the control narrowed keeps the 3 in its settings data
    and the picker has nowhere to show it. Same guard, same reason, as
    `sections/feature-cards.liquid`.

    `plus: 0` coerces the select's string first: `"2" > 2` compares a string to
    an integer, which is false in every Liquid.
  endcomment
  assign cols_mobile = s.columns_mobile | default: 1 | plus: 0
  if cols_mobile > 2
    assign cols_mobile = 2
  endif
  if cols_mobile < 1
    assign cols_mobile = 1
  endif

  assign cols_tablet = s.columns_tablet | default: 2 | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- the surface, from `sections/feature-cards.liquid` ----
  endcomment
  assign background_media = s.background_media | default: 'none'
  assign has_background_media = false
  if background_media != 'none'
    assign has_background_media = true
  endif

  assign background_paint = ''
  if has_background_media == false
    assign background_paint = s.background_color | default: ''
  endif

  comment
    Opacity goes into the colour rather than onto the element: `opacity` on the
    section would fade the cards along with the frame.

    With no colour picked the border is `currentColor`, which the colour filters
    cannot take an alpha channel from — there is nothing to read until the
    scheme resolves in the browser. `color-mix` does the same fade at that point
    instead, so both paths honour the slider.
  endcomment
  assign border_line = s.border_style | default: 'none'

  assign bw_top = 0
  assign bw_right = 0
  assign bw_bottom = 0
  assign bw_left = 0
  assign border_any = 0
  assign border_paint = ''

  if border_line != 'none'
    assign bw_top = s.border_width_top | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_right = s.border_width_right | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_bottom = s.border_width_bottom | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_left = s.border_width_left | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign border_any = bw_top | plus: bw_right | plus: bw_bottom | plus: bw_left

    assign border_percent = s.border_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    if s.border_color == blank
      assign border_paint = 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor ' | append: border_percent | append: '%, transparent)'
    else
      assign border_alpha = border_percent | divided_by: 100.0
      assign border_paint = s.border_color | color_modify: 'alpha', border_alpha
    endif
  endif

  assign radius = s.border_radius | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign radius_mobile = s.border_radius_mobile | default: radius | plus: 0
  assign margin_top = s.margin_top | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign margin_bottom = s.margin_bottom | default: 0 | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- the row ----

    Two column templates, one number. The intro panel publishes its own width as
    `--tc-intro-width` and the grid reads it, so the panel's slider is the only
    place the number is stated. `snippets/container.liquid` and the bleed below
    take care of where the row starts and ends.
  endcomment
  assign show_intro = s.show_intro
  if show_intro == nil
    assign show_intro = true
  endif

  comment
    `false == blank` is true in Liquid, so a blank check would read "off" as
    "not set" and turn the bleed back on. `nil` is the only value that means the
    merchant has not answered yet.
  endcomment
  assign bleed_end = s.carousel_bleed
  if bleed_end == nil
    assign bleed_end = true
  endif

  comment
    `plus: 0` rather than `default` alone on the mobile pair: 0 is a gap a merchant
    can legitimately want on a phone — cards flush against each other — and
    `default` would replace it with 16 every time.
  endcomment
  assign gap_x = s.gap_horizontal | default: 24 | plus: 0
  assign gap_y = s.gap_vertical | default: 24 | plus: 0

  assign gap_x_mobile = s.gap_horizontal_mobile | plus: 0
  if s.gap_horizontal_mobile == nil
    assign gap_x_mobile = 16
  endif
  assign gap_y_mobile = s.gap_vertical_mobile | plus: 0
  if s.gap_vertical_mobile == nil
    assign gap_y_mobile = 16
  endif

  assign row_gap = s.intro_gap | default: 32 | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- the carousel ----

    Two types, two answers, resolved exactly as `sections/feature-cards.liquid`
    resolves them. Only `carousel` reaches `data-layout`, or the component would
    try to build a Swiper out of a layout that is not one.

    The default is Carousel rather than Grid — the row is drawn against a fixed
    intro panel and running past the edge of the page — but Grid is a real
    option: it drops the bleed, wraps the cards into columns beside the panel
    and stands the controls down.
  endcomment
  assign layout_type = s.layout | default: 'carousel'

  assign cs_layout = 'grid'
  if layout_type == 'carousel'
    assign cs_layout = 'carousel'
  endif

  comment
    `false == blank` is true in Liquid, so a blank check would read "off" as
    "not set" and turn the mobile carousel back on. `nil` is the only value that
    means the merchant has not answered yet.
  endcomment
  assign carousel_on_mobile = s.carousel_on_mobile
  if carousel_on_mobile == nil
    assign carousel_on_mobile = true
  endif

  assign cs_layout_mobile = 'grid'
  if layout_type == 'carousel' or carousel_on_mobile
    assign cs_layout_mobile = 'carousel'
  endif

  assign cs_is_carousel = false
  if cs_layout == 'carousel' or cs_layout_mobile == 'carousel'
    assign cs_is_carousel = true
  endif

  comment
    The slide count, and only the slides.

    `carousel-options` uses it to decide whether the merchant's Loop setting is
    achievable — Swiper silently disables looping below twice `slidesPerView`,
    which reads as the setting doing nothing. So it has to be the number of
    cards, not `section.blocks.size`: an app block sitting in the row would
    inflate the number and let a loop through that Swiper then refuses.
  endcomment
  assign cs_count = 0
  for review_block in section.blocks
    if review_block.type == '_testimonial-card'
      assign cs_count = cs_count | plus: 1
    endif
  endfor

  assign cs_label = 'accessibility.carousel' | t

  comment
    ---- the controls, outside the track ----
  endcomment
  assign carousel_id = 'testimonials-' | append: section.id

  assign cs_pagination = s.carousel_pagination | default: 'controls'
  assign cs_pagination_align = s.carousel_pagination_align | default: 'center'

  assign cs_nav = s.carousel_navigation
  if cs_nav == nil
    assign cs_nav = true
  endif

  comment
    `controls` is one bar carrying its own arrows, so the bare pair below would
    be a duplicate of what it already draws — the same test
    `carousel-shell-tail` makes when the controls are nested.
  endcomment
  comment
    Whether the row is drawn at all is a Liquid question, not a runtime one. The
    layout is known here for both breakpoints, so the visibility is a class and
    a media query rather than a `:has()` test — and a progress bar can never be
    left on a page where the cards are a static grid.
  endcomment
  assign has_controls = false
  if cs_is_carousel and cs_nav or cs_is_carousel and cs_pagination != 'none'
    assign has_controls = true
  endif

  assign controls_class = 'testimonials__controls testimonials__controls--' | append: cs_pagination_align
  if cs_layout == 'carousel'
    assign controls_class = controls_class | append: ' testimonials__controls--always'
  elsif cs_layout_mobile == 'carousel'
    assign controls_class = controls_class | append: ' testimonials__controls--mobile'
  endif

  comment
    ---- the product disc ----

    Stated here rather than on the card, and inherited by every card, because
    the section is the only element that can reserve room for it: the disc hangs
    past the bottom of the card and swiper.css gives the carousel element
    `overflow: hidden`. The track's bottom padding and the disc's overhang are the
    same number, so they are the same setting.

    `blocks/_testimonial-card.liquid` documents the other half of this.
  endcomment
  assign thumb_size = s.thumb_size | default: 80 | plus: 0
  assign thumb_overhang = s.thumb_overhang | default: 24 | plus: 0
  assign thumb_inset = s.thumb_inset | default: 28 | plus: 0

  assign thumb_line = s.thumb_border_style | default: 'dashed'
  assign thumb_width = 0
  assign thumb_paint = ''

  if thumb_line != 'none'
    assign thumb_width = s.thumb_border_width | default: 1 | plus: 0

    assign thumb_percent = s.thumb_border_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    if s.thumb_border_color == blank
      assign thumb_paint = 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor ' | append: thumb_percent | append: '%, transparent)'
    else
      assign thumb_alpha = thumb_percent | divided_by: 100.0
      assign thumb_paint = s.thumb_border_color | color_modify: 'alpha', thumb_alpha
    endif
  endif

  assign info_inset = s.info_inset | default: 28 | plus: 0
  assign info_gap = s.info_gap | default: 14 | plus: 0

  comment
    What the product picture does while a pointer is over the card.

    A select rather than a pair of toggles, and a percentage rather than a
    multiplier: the two effects animate the same `transform` on the same layer, so
    two controls able to ask for both would resolve to whichever declaration
    came last in the stylesheet. The scale is converted here — the stylesheet
    wants 1.12 and the schema stores a number a merchant can reason about.
  endcomment
  assign thumb_effect = s.thumb_hover_effect | default: 'zoom_in'
  assign thumb_scale = s.thumb_hover_scale | default: 112 | plus: 0
  assign thumb_scale = thumb_scale | divided_by: 100.0

  assign card_stagger = s.animation_stagger | default: 120 | plus: 0

  comment
    The accent the intro panel's numbers and the card's stars fall back to, so
    the two stay in step with the heading's highlight above without either
    knowing about the other.
  endcomment
  assign accent = s.accent_color | default: ''

  comment
    The bleed is per breakpoint, because it belongs to the carousel rather than
    to the section: a grid that runs off the side of the page is a row with its
    last column cut in half and no way to reach it. So each breakpoint gets the
    class only where that breakpoint is actually a slider.
  endcomment
  assign track_classes = 'testimonials__track'
  if bleed_end and cs_layout == 'carousel'
    assign track_classes = track_classes | append: ' testimonials__track--bleed-desktop'
  endif
  if bleed_end and cs_layout_mobile == 'carousel'
    assign track_classes = track_classes | append: ' testimonials__track--bleed-mobile'
  endif
-%}

{%- capture section_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', section: s, declarations: true -%}
  --tc-gap-x: {{ gap_x }}px;
  --tc-gap-y: {{ gap_y }}px;
  --tc-gap-x-mobile: {{ gap_x_mobile }}px;
  --tc-gap-y-mobile: {{ gap_y_mobile }}px;
  --tc-row-gap: {{ row_gap }}px;
  --testimonials-radius: {{ radius }}px;
  --testimonials-radius-mobile: {{ radius_mobile }}px;
  --testimonials-margin-block-start: {{ margin_top }}px;
  --testimonials-margin-block-end: {{ margin_bottom }}px;
  --testimonials-controls-gap: {{ s.carousel_controls_gap | default: 40 | plus: 0 }}px;
  --tc-thumb-size: {{ thumb_size }}px;
  --tc-thumb-overhang: {{ thumb_overhang }}px;
  --tc-thumb-inset: {{ thumb_inset }}px;
  --tc-info-inset: {{ info_inset }}px;
  --tc-info-gap: {{ info_gap }}px;
  {%- if thumb_effect != 'none' -%}
    --tc-thumb-scale: {{ thumb_scale }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if thumb_width > 0 -%}
    --tc-thumb-border-width: {{ thumb_width }}px;
    --tc-thumb-border-style: {{ thumb_line }};
    --tc-thumb-border-color: {{ thumb_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if border_any > 0 -%}
    --testimonials-border-width: {{ bw_top }}px {{ bw_right }}px {{ bw_bottom }}px {{ bw_left }}px;
    --testimonials-border-style: {{ border_line }};
    --testimonials-border-color: {{ border_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if background_paint != '' -%}
    background: {{ background_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if accent != '' -%}
    --tc-accent: {{ accent }};
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<div
  class="testimonials testimonials--thumb-{{ thumb_effect | replace: '_', '-' }} color-scheme-container color-{{ s.color_scheme | default: 'scheme-1' }}{% if has_background_media %} has-background-media{% endif %}"
  data-section-spacing
  {%- if s.stack_layer != blank and s.stack_layer != 'default' %} data-section-layer="{{ s.stack_layer }}"{% endif %}
  data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
  style="{{ section_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
>
  {%- if has_background_media -%}
    {% render 'background-media', settings: s %}
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="{% render 'container', width: s.container_width %}">
    {%- comment -%}
      The merchant's heading cluster, as a static block so it cannot be dragged
      into the row of reviews and cannot be deleted by accident. Same mechanism,
      same reason, as `sections/feature-cards.liquid`.

      `children: true` staggers the cluster's own parts — the pill, the heading,
      the paragraph — so the section opens as one cascade rather than as a wall
      of text arriving at once.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <motion-effect
      class="testimonials__header testimonials__header--{{ s.alignment | default: 'center' }}"
      {% render 'motion-attrs', kind: 'text', section: s, children: true %}
    >
      {% content_for 'block', type: 'section-header', id: 'testimonials-header' %}
    </motion-effect>

    {%- comment -%}
      The layout names its own type, because the intro panel behaves differently
      in each. Beside a carousel it stretches to the row — one line of cards, one
      panel the same height. Beside a *grid* the row is as tall as however many
      rows of cards there are, and a stretched panel becomes a column of empty
      colour with the heading marooned at the top of it. So Grid pins the panel
      to its own height instead.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="testimonials__layout testimonials__layout--{{ cs_layout }}{% if show_intro %} testimonials__layout--with-intro{% endif %}">
      {%- if show_intro -%}
        <motion-effect
          class="testimonials__intro"
          {% render 'motion-attrs', kind: 'image', section: s %}
        >
          {% content_for 'block', type: '_testimonial-intro', id: 'testimonials-intro' %}
        </motion-effect>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        One `<motion-effect>` for the whole row — see the note at the top on why
        the cards are found by selector rather than carrying an effect each.

        `kind: 'image'` rather than `'text'`: a review card is a panel and a
        photograph, and the text family's presets split their target into words
        and letters.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <motion-effect
        class="{{ track_classes }} testimonials__track--{{ cs_layout }}"
        {% render 'motion-attrs',
           kind: 'image',
           section: s,
           target: '.testimonial-card',
           stagger: card_stagger %}
      >
        <swiper-carousel
          {% render 'carousel-shell-attrs',
             settings: s,
             id: carousel_id,
             layout: cs_layout,
             layout_mobile: cs_layout_mobile,
             classes: 'testimonials__carousel',
             columns_desktop: desktop,
             columns_tablet: cols_tablet,
             columns_mobile: cols_mobile,
             count: cs_count %}
        >
          <div
            class="carousel-shell__track testimonials__grid"
            data-ref="track"
            {% if cs_is_carousel %}aria-label="{{ cs_label | escape }}"{% endif %}
          >
            {% content_for 'blocks' %}
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            `detached` keeps the pause button and the live region — both are
            found by ref and announced from inside the element — and stands the
            arrows and the pagination down so they can be rendered below the row
            instead. Without it the section would draw each of them twice.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {% render 'carousel-shell-tail',
             settings: s,
             layout: cs_layout,
             layout_mobile: cs_layout_mobile,
             detached: true %}
        </swiper-carousel>
      </motion-effect>
    </div>

    {%- if has_controls -%}
      <div class="{{ controls_class }}">
        {%- if cs_pagination == 'controls' -%}
          {% render 'carousel-controls',
             settings: s,
             carousel: carousel_id,
             align: cs_pagination_align %}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- if cs_nav -%}
            {% render 'carousel-nav',
               settings: s,
               carousel: carousel_id,
               position: 'bottom' %}
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if cs_pagination != 'none' -%}
            {% render 'carousel-pagination',
               style: cs_pagination,
               align: cs_pagination_align,
               carousel: carousel_id %}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.testimonials.name",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "_testimonial-card"
    },
    {
      "type": "@app"
    }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "alignment",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.label",
      "info": "t:sections.testimonials.settings.alignment.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "start",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "center",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "end",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__3.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "center"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.testimonials.headers.row"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:sections.testimonials.paragraphs.row"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "layout",
      "label": "t:shared.carousel.layout_type.label",
      "info": "t:shared.carousel.layout_type.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "grid",
          "label": "t:shared.carousel.layout_type.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "carousel",
          "label": "t:shared.carousel.layout_type.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "carousel"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "carousel_on_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.carousel.carousel_on_mobile.label",
      "info": "t:shared.carousel.carousel_on_mobile.info",
      "default": true,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout != 'carousel' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_intro",
      "label": "t:sections.testimonials.settings.show_intro.label",
      "info": "t:sections.testimonials.settings.show_intro.info",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "carousel_bleed",
      "label": "t:sections.testimonials.settings.carousel_bleed.label",
      "info": "t:sections.testimonials.settings.carousel_bleed.info",
      "default": true,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout == 'carousel' or section.settings.carousel_on_mobile }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "columns_desktop",
      "label": "t:shared.columns.desktop.label",
      "info": "t:sections.testimonials.settings.columns_desktop.info",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 6,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "columns_tablet",
      "label": "t:shared.carousel.columns_tablet.label",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 4,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "columns_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.carousel.columns_mobile.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "1",
          "label": "t:shared.carousel.columns_mobile.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "2",
          "label": "t:shared.carousel.columns_mobile.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "1"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "gap_device",
      "label": "t:sections.testimonials.settings.gap_device.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "desktop",
          "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__1.label"
        },
